    "hasAgenda": true,
    "summary": "The December 2 Telluride Housing Authority Subcommittee meeting has one substantive action item: a request from Lela and Jon Martin for an exception to the permitted capital improvement limits under their deed restriction, covering a proposed $160,000 roof replacement at 950 E. Colorado Avenue, Gold Run, Unit 3B. That figure is 57% of their original purchase price of $279,200 — well beyond the 30% absolute cap written into their older deed restriction. Staff recommends approval, conditioned on the Martins executing a new deed restriction under the current Guidelines, which replaced the hard cap with a more flexible exception process. If approved, the unit's maximum sale price would climb significantly, raising affordability-tier questions the subcommittee will need to weigh. The board also takes up minutes from the October 7 and November 18 meetings.",
