  {
    "source": "telluride",
    "sourceLabel": "Town of Telluride",
    "title": "Special Town Council",
    "date": "2026-12-04",
    "time": "10:00 AM",
    "location": "Hybrid/Rebekah Hall, 113 W Columbia Ave",
    "agendaUrl": "https://telluride-co.civicweb.net/Portal/MeetingInformation.aspx?Id=8324",
    "packetUrl": "https://telluride-co.civicweb.net/document/448285/",
    "link": "https://telluride-co.civicweb.net/Portal/MeetingInformation.aspx?Id=8324",
    "hasAgenda": true,
    "summary": "This special meeting is a single-item public hearing: Town Council sits as an appellate body to review a challenge to HARC's September 16, 2026 approval of a new construction project at 208 S Fir Street. The appellant, an adjacent property owner at 150 W Pacific Avenue, filed the appeal on September 30, 2026. At issue is a three-story, 34.88-foot addition behind a reconstructed historic Supporting structure — bringing the project to 5,033 sq ft on a 3,525 sq ft lot in the Commercial zone, within the Telluride Historic Landmark District. The core argument: HARC approved the building without ever formally determining which design guidelines govern it — whether the replica qualifies as a rated Supporting structure reconstruction (triggering subordination and height standards) or as new construction on a vacant lot. HARC also amended a sequencing condition from its 2021 demolition approval, and the appellant contends that amendment was made without the findings the Land Use Code requires. Council will hear both appeals.",
